From f708e2f51a5d0a8ddf6bbc1f6144b2db494f6bc4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Bates <help@batesai.org>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 10:59:23 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 4/8] Subject Mastery progress API and sm_progress table

functions/api/subjectmastery/[[path]].js implements the site half of the
Subject Mastery contract (subject-mastery repo, docs/CONTRACT.md):

  GET    /api/subjectmastery/me        signed-in state + name/email/avatar
  GET    /api/subjectmastery/progress  this member's progress map (401 if not)
  PUT    /api/subjectmastery/progress  upsert up to 500 items, returns the map
  DELETE /api/subjectmastery/progress  reset

Merge rule per lesson key, enforced in the upsert's ON CONFLICT ... WHERE:
last write wins on updatedAt, except that completed/known is never
replaced by in_progress. Items are validated before anything is written
(key regex, status enum, finite position 0-86400, updatedAt no more than
five minutes ahead), and a request applies whole or not at all. Rows go
16 per statement in one batch so a full PUT stays inside D1's 100
bound-parameter and 50-queries-per-invocation limits. Same-origin only:
no CORS, and a PUT/DELETE naming a foreign Origin is refused. Every
response is Cache-Control: no-store.

migrations/0001_sm_progress.sql creates the table (idempotent). Account
deletion now also clears sm_progress, so the migration must reach the
production database before this code does.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
